// Rotate the rendered UI. `deg` is the ABSOLUTE effective rotation of the GUI against
// the panel's scanout — Go has already composed it from the hwconfig mount rotation and
// the requested orientation offset, so the renderer just obeys. It rides its own arm
// rather than GlobalOptions because the tree only travels on a config change, while an
// accelerometer flip can happen at any moment; it is also part of the connect replay, so
// a reconnecting renderer lands the right way up before its first tree.
